---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionRail from '../components/SectionRail.astro';
const rail=[{id:'about-intro',title:'Intro'},{id:'engineer',title:'Engineer'},{id:'builder',title:'Builder'},{id:'outside-code',title:'Outside Code'},{id:'context',title:'Education / Context'},{id:'perspective',title:'Product Perspective'}];
const dimensions=[
  {id:'engineer',title:'Engineer',copy:'I’m a software engineer from Türkiye. I move between product decisions, architecture, backend, Android, and systems work according to what the product requires. I care more about owning the problem than defending a stack. Technology is useful when it gives the product the behavior, reliability, and clarity it needs. That often means working across layers instead of treating one layer as the whole job.'},
  {id:'builder',title:'Builder',copy:'I build independently and as part of Devonair. The interesting part is following a product beyond implementation: from an idea and its intent, through behavior and system boundaries, into execution and validation. Shared work stays shared; the goal is clear responsibility rather than inflated ownership. A product becomes coherent when those decisions continue to agree with one another.'},
  {id:'outside-code',title:'Outside code',copy:'Photography, video, music production, Linux, and experiments with new technology keep me close to both sides of a tool. Making things from the creator’s side changes how I think about media software, control, feedback, and the small frictions that decide whether a product becomes part of someone’s work. The systems side keeps the same questions grounded in ownership and reliability.'},
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About | Mehmet Arslanca" description="About Mehmet Arslanca: software engineer from Türkiye, independent builder, Devonair collaborator, and creator interested in media, Linux, and technology.">
  <SectionRail sections={rail}/>
  <header id="about-intro" class="container route-intro" data-section-anchor data-scroll-reveal><p class="label">About</p><h1>A product is more than its implementation.</h1><p>So is the person building it.</p></header>
  <div class="dimensions">{dimensions.map((dimension,index)=><section id={dimension.id} class="section container dimension" data-section-anchor aria-labelledby={`${dimension.id}-heading`}><span class="label" data-scroll-reveal>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h2 id={`${dimension.id}-heading`} data-scroll-reveal>{dimension.title}</h2><p data-scroll-reveal data-motion-lag=".035">{dimension.copy}</p></section>)}</div>
  <section id="context" class="section container context" data-section-anchor><div data-scroll-reveal><p class="label">Personal context</p><h2>Türkiye,<br/>software, media.</h2></div><div data-scroll-reveal><p>I study Web Programming at Istanbul University. Outside product work, photography, video, music production, Linux, and experiments with new technology keep my engineering perspective close to the creator’s side of tools.</p><dl><div><dt class="label">Based in</dt><dd>Türkiye</dd></div><div><dt class="label">Studying</dt><dd>Web Programming</dd></div><div><dt class="label">Environment</dt><dd>CachyOS / KDE Plasma / Wayland</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/engineering/">Engineering <span class="arrow">→</span></a></div></section>
  <section id="perspective" class="section container perspective" data-section-anchor><div data-scroll-reveal><p class="label">How I end up thinking about products</p><h2>The user is part of the system.</h2></div><div data-scroll-reveal><p>Experimenting with technology keeps exposing the same gap: a tool can technically do something and still be a poor product to live with. I keep returning to the awkward permission, the unclear failure, and the extra step that should not exist.</p><p>Product quality lives in those details. It is also why I do not want one framework or stack to define the work. The useful choice is the one that gives the person using the product a clearer, more dependable experience.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .route-intro{padding-block:clamp(6rem,11vw,11rem)}.route-intro h1{max-width:14ch;font-size:clamp(4rem,9vw,9rem);line-height:.9;margin:1.5rem 0 2rem}.route-intro>p:last-child{color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1.2rem}.dimensions{display:grid;gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,5rem)}.dimension{width:min(88%,72rem);display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem minmax(10rem,.55fr) minmax(20rem,1fr);gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,5rem);align-items:start}.dimension:nth-child(even){margin-left:auto;grid-template-columns:minmax(20rem,1fr) 3rem minmax(10rem,.55fr)}.dimension:nth-child(even)>span{grid-column:2}.dimension:nth-child(even)>h2{grid-column:3}.dimension:nth-child(even)>p{grid-column:1;grid-row:1}.dimension h2{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,5rem)}.dimension p{color:var(--text-muted);max-width:60ch}.context,.perspective{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.75fr 1.25fr;gap:4rem 10rem}.context h2,.perspective h2{font-size:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem);line-height:.95}.context>div:last-child,.perspective>div:last-child{max-width:58ch;color:var(--text-muted)}.context dl{display:grid;gap:1.5rem;margin:3rem 0}.context dd{margin:.25rem 0 0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.35rem;color:var(--text)}@media(max-width:760px){.dimension,.dimension:nth-child(even){width:100%;margin:0;grid-template-columns:2.25rem 1fr;gap:1.25rem}.dimension:nth-child(even)>span,.dimension:nth-child(even)>h2,.dimension:nth-child(even)>p{grid-column:auto;grid-row:auto}.dimension p,.dimension:nth-child(even)>p{grid-column:2}.context,.perspective{grid-template-columns:1fr}}@media(max-width:600px){.route-intro h1{font-size:3rem;line-height:.94}}
</style>
